	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 520.0, 82.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 2 — Wrangling

The pipeline runs left to right. ORDER MATTERS: profile first, then impute,
then handle outliers. Compare the Data Table at each stage.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(760.0, 90.0, 300.0, 176.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. In Impute, try 'Average/Most frequent', then
   'Model-based imputer'. Compare in Data Table.
2. In Outliers, switch between One-Class SVM and
   Local Outlier Factor. How many rows are dropped?
3. In Select Rows, keep only age &gt;= 25.
4. Save the result as credit_clean.tab.

QUESTION: is dropping the outliers here defensible?
Justify in one sentence -- see book section 2.7.2.</text>
	</annotations>
